    <string name="privacy_policy_body">TapeBack is an offline app. It has no internet permission, so it cannot send anything anywhere.\n\nWhat stays on your phone: your recordings, cassette labels and cover images, diary tags, time-capsule letters and app settings. They live in the app\'s private storage and are excluded from cloud backup and device transfer.\n\nWhat TapeBack never does: no accounts, no analytics, no ads, no crash reporting, no tracking and no speech-to-text.\n\nPermissions: the microphone is used only while you record. Notifications show recording controls and tell you when a time capsule opens.\n\nSharing: a recording leaves the app only when you share it, save it to your device or create a backup. Backups are plain .zip files written where you choose. Uninstalling TapeBack deletes everything it stored.</string>

    <!-- About -->
    <string name="about_title">About</string>
    <string name="about_version_build">Version %1$s · build %2$d</string>
    <string name="about_story_title">A tape deck, resurrected</string>
    <string name="about_story_body">Before voice notes there was the cassette recorder: a click of REC, the hum of the motor, a label written by hand. TapeBack brings that ritual back for a voice diary and letters to your future self, with modern recording that never loses a take.</string>
    <string name="about_inside">What\'s inside</string>
    <string name="about_feature_record">Background recording with pause, levels and a safe save on every stop</string>
    <string name="about_feature_deck">Spinning reels with real tape physics, VU meters and piano keys</string>
    <string name="about_feature_library">Cassettes with Side A and B, labels, shells and cover art</string>
    <string name="about_feature_diary">A diary by date with search, tags, favorites and streaks</string>
    <string name="about_feature_capsule">Time capsules that stay sealed until the day they open</string>
    <string name="about_feature_privacy">Completely offline. No account, no ads, no tracking</string>
    <string name="about_credits">Credits</string>
    <string name="about_licenses">Open-source licenses</string>
    <string name="about_licenses_body">Fonts and libraries that make TapeBack possible</string>
    <string name="about_licenses_text">Fonts\n• Bungee by David Jonathan Ross, SIL Open Font License 1.1\n• Space Grotesk by Florian Karsten, SIL Open Font License 1.1\n• VT323 by Peter Hull, SIL Open Font License 1.1\n• Permanent Marker by Font Diner, Apache License 2.0\n\nLibraries (Apache License 2.0)\n• Kotlin and kotlinx.coroutines\n• Android Jetpack: Compose, Material 3, Navigation, Lifecycle, Room, DataStore, WorkManager, Core SplashScreen\n• AndroidX Media3: ExoPlayer and MediaSession\n\nSounds\nEvery key click, motor whirr and eject clunk is synthesized on the device. No recorded samples are bundled.</string>
    <string name="about_made_by">Made with care by F7 Developer</string>
